# A declaration in code and the level it stands on (the book, #shadowing-levels; #call-frame-20261115: no write-back). In Code
# `int: x 2` and `int: x 3` stand on the root level of the code and work with the call's local of the visible name:
# D\x stays 10. In Inline `int: x 7` stands in the block of `if`, a nested level: it takes its own place and shadows
# the outer x until the block is left, so the read after the block gives 1 and Inline\x stays 1. seen is written
# through data\. Observation: explicit writes in sub: observe (#flush-receiver-contract; #call-frame-20261115).
# The bodies over that data are given by the structural link (step 21.7 K2, S3: no form of call substitutes a data):
# Code and Inline are written inside D and launched by the paths `D\Code()` and `D\Inline()`, over their parent;
# the write of Inline goes to its own slot by the record path `Inline\seen := x`. The former records
# `call(D Code)` and `call(Inline)` keep the positionals of [args, code] (D, or Inline alone, is the args actual);
# the substitution of DATA is removed, and they answer 5 on this scene.
Observed:
    int: seen 0
    int: inline_seen 0
end: Observed
D:
    int: seen 0
    int: pad 99
    int: x 10
    Code:
        data\seen := x
        int: x 2
        int: x 3
    end: Code
    Inline:
        int: pad 90
        int: x 1
        int: seen 0
        if: 1 (int: x 7)
        Inline\seen := x
    end: Inline
end: D
Main:
    D\Code()
    D\Inline()
    Observed\seen := D\seen
    Observed\inline_seen := D\Inline\seen
